# cpmtools definitions for the RC2014's compact flash card, as Grant Searle's
# CBIOS lays it out (cbios128.asm): sixteen 8 MB drives of 512 tracks, each
# track 32 sectors of 512 bytes -- 128 CP/M records -- 4K blocks, 512
# directory entries, drive n at n x 8 MB. Drive A alone reserves its first
# track, where the CP/M system sits (the monitor loads sectors 0-23 of it).
# cpmtools reads a `diskdefs` in the working directory before the system
# one, which is how test/run_rc2014_zex_test.py uses this.
diskdef rc2014-a
  seclen 512
  tracks 512
  sectrk 32
  blocksize 4096
  maxdir 512
  skew 0
  boottrk 1
  os 2.2
end
